WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.138
Let’s walk through RFIs.

00:00:02.138 --> 00:00:04.600
Use an RFI when the team needs a ruling,

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.550
clarification, or missing scenario fact.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.125
State one decision-blocking question with enough context to answer,

00:00:11.125 --> 00:00:14.150
and revise the same record if White Cell returns it

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:14.287
.

00:00:14.287 --> 00:00:16.887
On this slide, send a focused question to White

00:00:16.887 --> 00:00:19.850
Cell or revise the same RFI when it is returned

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.462
for clarification.

00:00:21.462 --> 00:00:25.087
In practice, use RFIs for rulings and missing scenario

00:00:25.087 --> 00:00:28.212
information, not for routine team discussion.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.610
When you are ready, use Open RFIs to move

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.085
to the live surface.

00:00:33.085 --> 00:00:35.785
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:35.935
.
